_width":null,"image_height":null,"content_item_id":null,"content_item_type":null},{"id":740,"title":"Financial Literacy content","content":"<span style=\"color: rgb(75, 85, 99); font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;, &quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;;\">Introducing financial literacy into the school curriculum empowers students with the knowledge and skills they need to make informed and responsible financial decisions throughout their lives. Understanding concepts like saving, budgeting, investing, taxes, loans, and digital payments at an early age helps students develop healthy money habits. It prepares them to manage their finances, avoid debt traps, and plan for future goals such as higher education, entrepreneurship, or retirement. Moreover, financially literate individuals are more likely to contribute positively to the economy and&nbsp;society.<\/span>","content_type":"text","image_path":null,"image_url":null,"link_url":null,"video_path":null,"video_url":null,"table_data":null,"accordion_data":null,"order":1,"is_active":true,"created_at":"2025-09-22T08:21:45.023000Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T08:21:45.023000Z","page_section_id":"1842","content_heading":"<ol class=\"inline-flex items-center space-x-1 md:space-x-2 rtl:space-x-reverse\" style=\"--tw-border-spacing-x: 0; --tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 \/ 0.5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 